## Transport (single adapter)

All endpoints speak `POST {base_url}/chat/completions` (OpenAI shape). Images go in as base64 `image_url` content blocks. `base_url` must be the API root that exposes `/chat/completions` (e.g. `https://api.openai.com/v1`, `http://localhost:11434/v1`). Local servers (Ollama, LM Studio, vLLM) and cloud (OpenAI, OpenRouter) all work; Anthropic/Gemini via an OpenAI-compat proxy.

- `llm_client.chat(config, system, user_text, images)` → `(text, info)` where `info = {usage, finish_reason, raw}`; raises `LLMError`. `_extract_message_text` tolerates content-as-blocks, reasoning-only replies, and completion-style `text`; a 200 body carrying an `error` is raised as `LLMError`. Both `chat` and `chat_messages` share `_post_chat`.
- `llm_client.chat_messages(config, messages, max_tokens?, temperature?, timeout?)` → `(text, info)` for **multi-turn** conversations with a pre-built OpenAI `messages` array. Used by the **AI Tools batch ops** (one-shot JSON is fine there). The optional `timeout` (seconds) overrides the endpoint's `timeout_seconds`.
- `llm_client.chat_messages_stream(config, messages, ...)` → **generator** yielding `{type:'delta', content, reasoning}` chunks then a single `{type:'done', text, reasoning, finish_reason, usage}`. Asks for `"stream": true`, parses OpenAI SSE (`data: {...}\n\n` / `[DONE]`). Used by the dashboard **Explain** tutor and the admin **Chat** console — streaming bytes flow continuously so reverse proxies don't cut the connection on long reasoning runs. Servers that ignore `stream:true` and return one-shot JSON are detected by `Content-Type` and yielded as a single `done` event (graceful fallback). Interactive routes pass `LLM_CHAT_TIMEOUT_SECONDS` (default 600 s) as the timeout. `_image_block(b64, mime)` builds an `image_url` content block.
- `llm_client.prepare_image(abs_path, max_dim)` → downscaled JPEG `(b64, mime)` for sending.
- `llm_client.read_image_data_uri(abs_path)` → ORIGINAL bytes data-URI (whole-image figure fallback).
- `llm_client.crop_image_data_uri(abs_path, box, pad, max_dim)` → PNG data-URI of a cropped region; `box` is `[x1,y1,x2,y2]` **fractions** 0..1 (top-left origin). Flattens alpha to white; raises `ValueError` for a degenerate box.
- `resolve_api_key(config)`: decrypt `api_key_enc` (Fernet) → else `os.getenv(api_key_env or 'LLM_API_KEY')`.

## API-key storage (hybrid)

Per-endpoint key entered in the UI is stored **Fernet-encrypted** in `LLMConfig.api_key_enc`; blank ⇒ fall back to `.env`. The Fernet key derives from `LLM_KEY_SECRET` (else `SECRET_KEY`) via SHA-256 → urlsafe-b64. **Rotating that secret invalidates stored ciphertexts** (re-enter keys). Plaintext keys are NEVER serialised to the browser — the data route reports only `has_stored_key` / `key_resolves`.

## SSE contract

Routes mirror `batch_generate_images`: gather work in request context, stream inside a pushed `app.app_context()`. Both ops are GET (EventSource) + `text/event-stream`.

- `GET /admin/questions/ai/check` — params `question_ids`, `endpoint_id`, `typed_version`, `ref_version`, `atypes` (csv QUE/ANS/SOL), `recheck` (1/0).
- `GET /admin/questions/ai/generate-md` — params `question_ids`, `endpoint_id`, `source_version`, `target_version`, `atypes`, `overwrite` (1/0), `embed_image` (1/0).
- `POST /admin/questions/ai/cancel` — body `{job_id}`.
- `GET /admin/questions/ai/endpoints` — enabled endpoints for the modal dropdown (subject-admin OK).
- `POST /admin/questions/<id>/assets/ai/generate-md` — **synchronous** (not SSE) per-slot MD generation for the edit-modal button; body `{version, asset_type, endpoint_id, embed_image?, overwrite?}` (source = target = `version`); returns `{success, status, message, asset_id}`.
- `POST /admin/questions/<id>/assets/check-state` — **manual** set/clear of a slot's proofread status; body `{version, asset_type, state, note?, severity?}` where `state ∈ ok|issues|error|clear`. Writes check fields to ALL rows in the slot; `clear` nulls them. Manual edits store `checked_by: "manual"` + `editor` username. Drives the editable status bar.

Event dicts: `{type, message, current?, total?, ...}`. `type` ∈ `job` (first; carries `job_id`) / `info` / `skip` / `success` / `error` / `done`. The `done` event carries `stats` (`{ok, issues, skipped, errors}` for check; `{created, skipped, errors}` for MD).

## Cancellation (real server-side Stop)

`app/ai_tools._AI_CANCEL: {job_id: threading.Event}`. Each generator checks the flag **between questions** and emits a final `done`. The frontend Stop posts the `job_id` (captured from the `job` event) and keeps the stream open so the final `done` arrives. Single-process assumption (same caveat as the settings hot-reload): the cancel POST must reach the worker running the stream.

## Check-state semantics

`iter_check` loads all IMG parts of the typed slot + reference slot; skips (with event) if either missing, or if already checked and `recheck` is off. Sends reference images first, then typed; parses strict JSON via `ai_prompts.parse_check_result`. Writes the SAME `check_state`/`check_result`/`checked_at` to every typed IMG part. States: `ok` (faithful), `issues` (discrepancies listed), `error` (unparseable reply — raw stored). `check_result` JSON: `{status, issues:[{severity,location,description}], model, ref_version, checked_by}` (manual edits use `checked_by:"manual"` + `editor`).

The edit-modal slot header keeps a compact badge (`renderCheckBadge`), and the IMG group shows a prominent **editable** status bar (`renderCheckStatusBar`, shown whenever the slot has images — even unchecked): colour-coded OK/issues/error/"Not proofread", the issue list, and inline **mark correct / mark issue… / clear** buttons (`setSlotCheckState` → `set_asset_check_state`). All of this is gated on `window.OQB_AI_TOOLS_ENABLED` (admin + dashboard).

## MD generation

`generate_md_slot(question, atype, source_version, target_version, ...)` is the **shared single-slot worker** (returns `{status: created|updated|skip|error, message, asset_id?}`). `iter_generate_md` loops it per slot and maps results to SSE events; the synchronous `ai_generate_md_slot` route calls it once.

Per slot: load source IMG parts → `MD_SYSTEM` LLM call → `strip_md_fences` → `normalize_inline_math` (tightens `$ x $` → `$x$` so pandoc/docx renders it — `tex_math_dollars` rejects spaced inline delimiters; the prompt also asks for tight `$x$`). **Figures are only embedded when the transcription actually contains a `[FIGURE: ...]` placeholder** (`ai_prompts.FIGURE_RE` / `figure_captions`) — pure-text questions yield Markdown only, no image. When figures exist and `embed_image` is on, `_embed_figures` runs a **second LLM "locate figures" pass** (`FIGURE_BOX_SYSTEM` → `parse_figure_boxes`, fractional boxes) for single-image slots and replaces each placeholder with a **cropped** base64 image (`crop_image_data_uri`); it falls back to the **whole** source image when the box is missing/degenerate/near-full-page (`_box_is_useful`) or the slot has multiple parts. Skips+logs if the result exceeds `MD_MAX_SIZE_BYTES`. Writes to the canonical MD path (`_md_rel_path`, mirrors `admin.create_md_asset`), upserts the target `QuestionAsset`, and calls `md_render.invalidate(asset.id)`.

The prompt is strict that `[FIGURE]` is ONLY for real diagrams/graphs/drawings — never plain text, equations, tables, or MC options.

## Explain (AI tutor chat — dashboard, all users)

`POST /dashboard/api/question/<id>/explain` (login-required, gated on `AI_TOOLS_ENABLED`, subject-access checked via `has_subject_access`) drives the dashboard **Explain** button. Unlike the admin AI Tools, it's available to **any** logged-in user with access to the subject, and uses the **default endpoint** — `_default_explain_endpoint()` first honours the `EXPLAIN_DEFAULT_LLM` system setting (an endpoint name picked from a dropdown of enabled endpoints), and falls back to the first enabled, vision-capable `LLMConfig` by `sort_order,name` when the setting is blank or names a missing/disabled endpoint.

- Body `{turns: [{role,content}], version_priority?}`. `turns` is the conversation AFTER the (server-built) initial image turn; empty for the first request. Stateless: the server rebuilds turn 1 (system `EXPLAIN_SYSTEM` + labelled QUE/SOL context) every call and appends `turns`, so images aren't re-uploaded from the browser.
- `_explain_slot_context(qid, atype, vp, ...)` prefers IMG (vision) via `_resolve_preview_assets(..., force_format='IMG')`; falls back to the slot's MD **text** when no image exists. QUE is required (image or MD); SOL is optional.
- **Response is `text/event-stream`** (SSE). Events: `{type:'preamble'}` (sent immediately so proxies see bytes) → zero-or-more `{type:'delta', content?, reasoning?}` (live tokens) → either `{type:'done', reply, reply_html, model, endpoint, has_solution}` or `{type:'error', message}`. `reply_html` is `md_render.render_text(normalize_inline_math(reply))` (sanitised; KaTeX client-side). Response headers set `X-Accel-Buffering: no` (nginx flush) and `Cache-Control: no-cache`. `chat_messages_stream` sets `resp.encoding = 'utf-8'` before iterating because LM Studio and several Ollama builds omit `charset=utf-8` and `requests` would otherwise fall back to ISO-8859-1 → mojibake on curly quotes / CJK / emoji.
- Frontend lives in `templates/dashboard.html` (`_explainStreamRequest`): reads `response.body.getReader()`, parses SSE blocks, accumulates content + reasoning, renders both live (reasoning in a `<details>` disclosure, content via `window.oqbRenderMarkdownLive` which runs `marked` over the buffer with KaTeX pre-rendered), then on `done` swaps the bubble to the server-rendered (bleach-sanitised) Markdown HTML and runs `oqbTypesetMath`. Raw `reply` is stored in `turns` for the next request.

## Direct chat (super-admin endpoint console)

`POST /admin/llm-endpoints/<id>/chat` is a **raw** chat console on the LLM Endpoints management page (super-admin only). Body `{turns: [{role, content}, ...]}` is passed straight to `llm_client.chat_messages_stream(cfg, messages)` with **no system prompt, no injected context, and no other guardrails** — useful for probing model behaviour, debugging Markdown formatting, or sanity-checking a newly added endpoint before exposing it via the AI Tools / Explain flows.

Same SSE contract as Explain (`preamble`/`delta`/`done`/`error`); the reply is `normalize_inline_math`'d and Markdown-rendered server-side at end-of-stream so KaTeX in the chat bubbles works the same way as the dashboard. Disabled endpoints are rejected with a 400. The server caps each message at 16 KiB and the running transcript at the most recent 40 turns. UI lives in `templates/admin_llm_endpoints.html` (`#chatModal`, `openChatModal`, `sendChatMessage`).

## Gotchas / invariants

1. Whole feature gated on `AI_TOOLS_ENABLED`; image ops require `supports_vision`.
2. Subject-admins may run on their own subjects only — `question_ids` is intersected with `get_user_admin_subjects()` (same as the batch ops). Endpoint CRUD is super-admin only.
3. LLM JSON is unreliable — `parse_check_result` extracts fenced/bare JSON defensively and returns `None` on total failure (caller stores raw + `check_state='error'`).
4. Images are downscaled to `LLM_IMAGE_MAX_DIM` (long edge) before sending; embedded MD figures use the original bytes.
5. The dev server must run threaded for the long SSE streams (already the case for the other batch ops).
